00:00:23.773 --> 00:00:24.774
101 take one.

00:00:24.774 --> 00:00:26.192
Common mark A and B.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.527
A and B common mark.

00:00:31.614 --> 00:00:34.492
When I was growing up,
I loved Slasher movies.

00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:36.619
Good morning, 
ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:36.619 --> 00:00:39.706
Horror films have a 
very complicated relationship

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.875
with gender and sexual identity.

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:44.627
I can't make you straight,
but you give us this week.

00:00:44.627 --> 00:00:45.712
We might be able to help.

00:00:48.298 --> 00:00:51.301
What I wanted to do was 
take the tropes of the Slasher movie

00:00:52.177 --> 00:00:54.429
and use them for gay celebration.

00:00:54.429 --> 00:00:56.681
Boys' cabin over there. Girls'
cabin over there.

00:00:56.681 --> 00:00:58.349
I use they/them pronouns.

00:00:58.349 --> 00:01:00.643
As in, they can't believe 
they're at this fucking camp.

00:01:01.269 --> 00:01:04.689
I've started in Slasher films 
 over a really long time ago.

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:10.028
What's really brilliant about 
what John has done with the script is

00:01:10.028 --> 00:01:14.908
to take a fairly traditional 
camp Slasher movie.

00:01:15.492 --> 00:01:18.578
- Who is that? 
- And layer on top of that.

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:19.829
- Come in, please.

00:01:19.829 --> 00:01:23.541
- Is the horror of a place
that believes that they can

00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:26.961
convert people with 
 pseudo therapy techniques.

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:30.757
It's scary because 
"conversion therapy" is abuse,

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:33.426
and it is torture that messes
with your entire being.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.096
Do you think your parents 
are disappointed in you?

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.388
Sometimes. 

00:01:37.388 --> 00:01:38.473
So what do you do?

00:01:38.473 --> 00:01:41.392
You try to make yourself special.

00:01:41.392 --> 00:01:43.436
You become...

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:44.646
They.

00:01:45.188 --> 00:01:46.272
I think we're bringing awareness

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:49.150
to what's actually 
 happening in the world.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.361
- It's time to play.

00:01:51.361 --> 00:01:53.446
-To hopefully bring 
 an end to the

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:55.073
horror that happens 
 at these camps.

00:01:57.867 --> 00:02:00.870
I have zero interest 
 in not being gay.

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:02.956
There's no judgments 
in this room.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.875
-When it came to 
casting the seven campers,

00:02:05.875 --> 00:02:07.001
it was very important to me

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:08.795
to cast queer actors.

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:10.964
- Sometimes I wish I was invisible.

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:14.092
- Because, we have 
 been so underrepresented

00:02:14.092 --> 00:02:15.552
in terms of playing ourselves.

00:02:15.552 --> 00:02:20.932
- John said, I would like to have
young people who identify

00:02:20.932 --> 00:02:23.434
with any one of these campers 

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:26.396
and root for someone 
 that they see in themselves.

00:02:26.396 --> 00:02:28.815
I am a gay 
 Korean-American woman.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:32.110
I am so grateful and honored  
to be a part of a movie

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:36.239
that has authentic representation
told by authentic storytellers.

00:02:36.239 --> 00:02:41.202
The best way that we can assure
we are making the best art

00:02:41.202 --> 00:02:46.875
is to include as many and as diverse
a population of people possible.

00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:49.294
Every single character represents  

00:02:49.294 --> 00:02:53.298
a different section
of the queer experience.

00:02:53.298 --> 00:02:55.550
- I know what I am? 
What are you?

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:57.135
It's just a different environment.

00:02:57.135 --> 00:02:58.511
I haven't seen before.

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:01.973
Finding my own truth
and celebrating my uniqueness.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.437
The most important
thing to remember is

00:03:07.437 --> 00:03:08.813
it's an entertaining movie.

00:03:08.813 --> 00:03:10.732
I didn't set out to write a lecture.

00:03:10.732 --> 00:03:12.692
If you love Horror movies,

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.861
if you love human
drama and thrillers,

00:03:15.945 --> 00:03:16.821
this is the movie for you.

00:03:16.821 --> 00:03:18.615
- This should be cozy.

00:03:18.615 --> 00:03:21.117
To even see this 
concept manifest on screen

00:03:21.117 --> 00:03:23.536
I think that John is a genius.

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:26.581
- Today, we're going to be exploring
traditional gender roles.

00:03:26.581 --> 00:03:28.958
We are creating something
completely new here,

00:03:28.958 --> 00:03:31.252
and I don't have 
a comparison in my head.

00:03:31.628 --> 00:03:33.796
We subvert a lot
 of Slasher tropes.

00:03:33.796 --> 00:03:34.505
-AHHH!

00:03:34.964 --> 00:03:36.466
So I'm like, What's going to happen?

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:38.343
Taste?

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:40.178
We need to get out of here.

00:03:40.178 --> 00:03:41.721
What are we supposed to do?
We're trapped.

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:43.223
There's going to 
be a lot of surprises.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.850
- And I think it'll 
get people talking.

00:03:46.684 --> 00:03:48.519
Shhh.

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:51.731
AHHHH!

